  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1100 PM MST Wed Nov 18 2026\n\nCurrently, there is an upper level shortwave ridge that is parked\nover the Mountain West. This is bringing us some high clouds and \ndry conditions with some fog possible remaining over Hudspeth \ncounty. However, as we get into the weekend, a strong positively \ntilted upper level Pacific trough will make its way into the \nregion. The models differ in terms of exact timing and location, \nwith the GFS favoring a deeper and slower- moving trough. \nRegardless, the greatest chances for precip will be downstream of \nthe trough in the right exit region over the Sacramento and Gila \nmountain ranges. With the frontal passage expected Saturday \nafternoon and evening, winds should shift from the Southwest to \nthe Northwest generally between 10 to 15 kts. \n\nThrough the rest of the period into Wednesday, a shortwave ridge \nwill move through region bringing drier air through Monday late \nafternoon and northeast winds. An upper level shortwave trough \nwill follow through early Tuesday morning, bringing an increase \nwith winds generally from the South and Southeast. However, little\nprecipitation is expected during this period through Wednesday.",
